hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16822","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from al-A'mash from Ya'qub ibn Buhayr from Dirar ibn al-Azwar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while he was milking, and said: Leave the caller of the milk."
"16823","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, our neighbor, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Bahili al-Athram al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Sulayman the reciter narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to us from Abu Wa'il from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Stretch out your hand that I may pledge allegiance to you upon Islam. Dirar said: Then I said: I have left the divining arrows and the playing of the singing girls and wine in fervent prayer and supplication, and my charging with the inscribed blade in the thick of battle, and my carrying war against the polytheists. O Lord, let my bargain not be a loss, for I have sold my wealth and my family in exchange. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your bargain has not been a loss, O Dirar."
"16824","Abd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to me, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Ya'qub ibn Buhayr from Dirar ibn al-Azwar, he said: My family sent me with a milch camel to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered me to milk it, and I milked it, and he said: Leave the caller of the milk."
"16825","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to me, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us from al-A'mash from Amr ibn Murra from al-Mughira ibn Sa'd from his father or from his uncle, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafa, and I took hold of the rein of his she-camel or its halter, and they pushed me away from him, and he said: Leave him, for he has a need that brought him. And I said: Inform me of a deed that brings me near to Paradise and distances me from the Fire. He said: And he raised his head to the sky, then he said: If you have been brief in asking, you have asked for something great, or long: Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, and establish the prayer, and give the zakat, and perform pilgrimage to the House, and fast Ramadan, and come to people with what you love that they bring to you, and what you dislike for yourself, leave the people from it. Let go of the rein of the she-camel."
